{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>For he will not forgive your transgression.</b> Every place where he is dispatched he carries out his mission, but he cannot show favoritism, as it is written: ישא ה' פניו etc. — and not an angel — כי שמי בקרבו. Therefore I warn you not to rebel against him, as though you are rebelling against me, because my name is within him. And he will not be able to forgive your transgression, for the forgiveness depends on me. A parable: to one who rebels against the word of the treasurer, who has no power to grant pardon, for pardons depend on the king. And Rashi explained כי שמי בקרבו — this is Metatron, whose name is like the name of his master, for Metatron has the numerical value of Shaddai. And a support for this: כי שמי בקרבו — remove the yod from שמי and there remains ש\"ד; and the bet and qof of בקרבו, by the atbash cipher, give שדי together with the yod of שמי; and from the word בקרבו there remains for you the name of his master. And Rabbi Moshe says: therefore I say of him that his name is like the name of his master, because his name is called in the alpha-beta of Rabbi Akiva, where it enumerates 72 names that he has."], :book :exodus, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:04:01.374535974Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}